---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../../data/site';
---

<Base
  title="About — Kaiming Yi"
  description="Kaiming Yi (gameKnife) — graphics and game engine engineer. 15 years in real-time rendering, currently at Perfect World, previously Tencent TiMi."
>
  <div class="shell-narrow wrap">
    <div class="marker">About</div>
    <h1>Kaiming Yi</h1>

    <div class="prose">
      <p class="lede">
        I am a graphics and game engine engineer based in Chengdu, China. Seventeen years writing code,
        fifteen of them in real-time graphics — and I expect to keep going for a while.
      </p>

      <h2>Two threads</h2>
      <p>
        My mother wanted me to play piano; I wanted to be a painter. Neither happened, and I ended up
        writing code instead — but <strong>the art thread never got cut</strong>. Charcoal and oil studies,
        then CG stills (one of them took a CGTalk Editor&rsquo;s Choice in 2009), and now renderers.
        It is the same question throughout: <strong>what does light do when it hits something</strong>.
        Only the instrument changed, from brush to GPU.
      </p>

      <h2>Now</h2>
      <p>
        Technical Expert at Perfect World&rsquo;s TZY Studio — infrastructure, technology selection, and
        the hard problems on a new project. Before that, eight years at Tencent TiMi Studios (T11),
        shipping <em>Let&rsquo;s Hunt Monsters</em> and <em>Saint Seiya</em>, plus two titles that never
        made it out.
      </p>
      <p>
        Evenings and weekends go to <a href="/engine/">gkNextEngine</a> — a C++20 + Vulkan real-time path
        tracing engine started in May 2024, with first-party code deliberately capped at 50k lines.
      </p>

      <h2>What I do well</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Real-time rendering</strong> — Vulkan, path tracing, GPU-driven pipelines, upscaling and denoising</li>
        <li><strong>Engine architecture</strong> — ECS, reflection, scripting runtimes, cross-platform RHI</li>
        <li><strong>Performance work</strong> — low-end device optimization, hard crash triage, CI and build throughput</li>
        <li><strong>Technical art</strong> — formal art training, fluent with art pipelines and TA workflows</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Get in touch</h2>
      <p>
        <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> ·
        <a href="https://github.com/gameknife" rel="me noopener" target="_blank">GitHub</a> ·
        <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/kaimingyi" rel="me noopener" target="_blank">LinkedIn</a>
      </p>

      <p class="note">
        Full CV at <a href="/en/cv/">/en/cv/</a>. Most of the writing on this site is in Chinese —
        the <a href="/blog/">blog</a> goes back to 2013.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .wrap { padding-block: 3.5rem 2rem; }
  h1 { font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 5vw, 2.6rem); margin: .5rem 0 2rem; }
  .lede { font-size: 1.08rem; color: var(--text) !important; }
  .note { font-size: .88rem; color: var(--muted) !important; padding-top: 1.2rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line-soft); }
</style>
